WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.979 --> 00:00:01.979
OK.

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:03.740
Another question that came in, David.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:07.660
Joe Biden is expected to select his vice president
around August 1st.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.519
Who do you think would hurt Biden the most?

00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:13.370
So earlier know when was it?

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.370
Last week.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:18.949
I said that I believe Elizabeth Warren should
be Joe Biden's vice presidential pick.

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:22.599
This is a different question, not who would
be best, but who would be worst.

00:00:22.599 --> 00:00:27.410
So the first thing is to understand what is
the goal of selecting a vice president?

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:29.760
There's essentially two goals.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.809
One, don't cause a problem for the presidential
candidate.

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:38.400
So Sarah Palin did did not help John McCain
back in 2008.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:43.739
Now, McCain was already losing, but Palin
was a cartoonish sideshow and certainly did

00:00:43.739 --> 00:00:44.980
not help.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.320
And number two, can you increase the electorate?

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:55.359
Can you bring in some additional people to
bolster support for the presidential candidate?

00:00:55.359 --> 00:00:57.940
So you look at someone like Paul Ryan.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:02.809
Paul Ryan didn't do much one way or the other
for Romney in terms of creating scandals are

00:01:02.809 --> 00:01:05.030
saying crazy things.

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:10.190
Arguably, Paul Ryan maybe helped Romney a
little bit when it comes to the electorate

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:11.190
being from where it was.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.230
Ryan from Virginia.

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:16.910
I think Romney being, you know, a massive
former Massachusetts governor, maybe not didn't

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.330
really do much one way or the other.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:22.900
Mike Pence didn't do much for Trump in terms
of bad news headlines.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.590
He just stayed out of the way.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:26.570
But maybe Pence helped in the Midwest.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:30.640
Maybe Pence helped with the evangelical vote,
which ultimately mostly went to Donald Trump

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:31.640
anyway.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:35.230
I believe if Joe Biden were to choose Hillary
Clinton, it would probably be bad.

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:37.490
That would probably hurt him.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:42.750
If Joe Biden were to choose, you know, an
actual Republican, if Joe Biden announces,

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:47.360
I don't know, Ted Cruz is my running mate,
I think it's a real problem for Biden.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.790
I think that.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.400
But obviously, he's not going to do that.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:55.530
And if Joe Biden picks someone with a lot
of baggage that can be attacked, that would

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:56.530
be a problem.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:02:02.360
So, for example, Amy Klobuchar, it was revealed
in the aftermath of the killing of George

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:07.420
Floyd that she had been involved in decisions
not to go after Derek Schavan, who ultimately

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:11.709
is the officer that killed George Floyd with
the need of the neck.

00:02:11.709 --> 00:02:17.659
Once that went public, it was obvious that
Clowe, Bashar was damaged in terms of a vice

00:02:17.659 --> 00:02:18.750
presidential candidate.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:21.810
She came out and said, I'm dropping out because
it should be a woman of color.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:25.140
But it was clear at that point she wasn't
going to be selected anyway.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.950
That type of baggage could be damaging to
Joe Biden.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:29.280
Obviously, it's not going to be close, Bashar.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.490
Now, I've got a couple e-mails from people
who said the Native American thing would be

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.560
baggage for Elizabeth Warren.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:35.560
I don't know that it would.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:36.950
I really don't know that it would.

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.659
I think, listen, if you want to talk about
baggage.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:45.950
Kamala Harris, his record is California attorney
general prosecuting the war on drugs and putting

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.959
a lot of black folks in jail, in prison, in
prison.

00:02:49.959 --> 00:02:55.180
I think that that may be baggage that Biden
does not need, but I may be wrong there.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:03:01.019
So, again, the point here is when you pick
a V.P., you want someone who's not going to

00:03:01.019 --> 00:03:04.500
get a ton of attention because typically it
will be negative attention.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:11.049
Number two, you want someone who maybe can
help you in terms of expanding your base of

00:03:11.049 --> 00:03:12.159
support.

00:03:12.159 --> 00:03:16.540
And number three, you want someone who's not
going to bring some kind of baggage that is

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:22.700
going to disproportionately become subject
matter for discussion if you disagree with

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:23.700
me.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:24.700
Let me know.

